To disable it just change this:
	TargetProcess.Write<DebugFilter>(debugsettings + 0x1c, DebugFilter::Dynamic);
To:
	TargetProcess.Write<DebugFilter>(debugsettings + 0x1c, DebugFilter::Off);

Additionally, if you want to do it even easier without restarting the program, go into your game settings and turn occlusion culling off. Then when you turn it back on it will appear again.
